All upstream file-level copyright and license notices remain in that archive.
NVIDIA Corporation holds copyright in contributed build/GPU infrastructure
with Apache-2.0 notices; see FAISS-APACHE-LICENSE for that license text. These
components are retained as source, not compiled by the CPU fallback.
The package compiles only its generic CPU library, not Python or GPU code.
The documented r-compat.patch supplies static Windows linkage and converts
FAISS fatal assertions/output errors to C++ exceptions for embedding in R,
corrects compiler compatibility diagnostics and quantizer initialization order,
and removes unused global C RNG
seeding. The package-local console adapter buffers FAISS diagnostics for R's
console without calling R's API from FAISS worker threads.
See src/vendor/README for provenance, checksum and build details.

CUDA, cuVS, OpenMP and numerical libraries are external dependencies and are
not included in the bundled archive. Linking to them does not transfer their
copyright to the faissR authors.
